# Conventions

Add a bullet only after it is a real project habit. Do not paste a style guide.

## Repository

- Project rules are `.mdc` files under `.cursor/rules/` (nested folders are fine).
- Skills live at `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with `name` matching the folder.
- Secrets stay out of git. Use `.env` locally and `${env:NAME}` in `.cursor/mcp.json`.
- Godot project lives in `game/` so the editor does not import backend/tool files.
- Branches: `main` (always green), `phase/NN-short-name`, `fix/...`, `chore/...`.
- Conventional Commits: `feat(combat): …`, `fix(net): …`, `test(items): …`, `docs(scope): …`, `chore(ci): …`.
- One BUILD_SCOPE task = one commit. Do not commit `.godot/`, `export/`, `build/`, `.env`, or user saves.

## Skyrope (from BUILD_SCOPE §8)

- Typed GDScript everywhere. Treat `untyped_declaration` as an error. Tabs in `*.gd`; 2 spaces in JSON/YAML.
- `.gd` hard limit 400 lines (aim 250). Functions ≤ 50 lines. One responsibility per script.
- `sim/` never references `client/`, UI, audio, camera, `Input`, or the `Net` autoload.
- `client/` never mutates sim entities. Presentation reads Authority snapshots/events and `GameState`.
- If a designer would tweak a number, it belongs in `game/data/*.json`, not code.
- Discover data only via `game/data/index.json`. Never `DirAccess` for content files.
- No `MultiplayerSynchronizer` / `MultiplayerSpawner`. Custom snapshots only.
- Original names and art only. No MapleStory/Nexon assets, names, or private-server dumps.
- Tests accompany `game/sim/` and `game/shared/` logic. Never delete tests to go green.
- After each task: headless boot + GUT. Tick the BUILD_SCOPE checkbox only when that passes.
- First Godot launch on a machine: `godot --headless --import --path game` (or open `game/` in the editor) before Play. Windows PowerShell: prefix quoted exe paths with `&`. No `make` unless Git Bash/WSL provides it.

## Starter habits still useful

- **Smoke before done:** `verify-godot-change` for game code; `npm run verify` after Cursor layout changes.
- Keep the `assets/` catalog. Do not install hooks unless the user asked.

